# PNJC Liquidity Locker V2

PNJC Liquidity Locker V2 is an immutable smart contract for locking Uniswap V2 LP tokens.

## Scope

This contract is designed to custody-lock a single Uniswap V2-style ERC-20 LP token for a fixed period of time.

It is **not** an ERC-20 PNJC token contract.

It does **not** mint, burn, rebase, tax, or otherwise manage PNJC supply.

It does **not** support Uniswap V3 NFT positions.

Its only purpose is to hold LP tokens in a transparent and time-locked manner until the unlock timestamp is reached.

## Security Model

- No owner.
- No admin role.
- No upgradeability.
- No emergency withdrawal.
- No rescue functions.
- Reentrancy protection on all state-changing functions.
- Deterministic unlock logic based on block timestamp.
- Immutable LP token address configured at deployment.

## Supported Asset Type

- Uniswap V2 LP token (ERC-20)

## Key Design Principles

- Simple custody model.
- Explicit on-chain lock records.
- Withdrawals allowed only after the unlock time.
- Minimal trusted surface area.
- Clear and indexer-friendly event emissions.

## Public Interface

- `lock(amount, beneficiary, unlockTime)`
- `withdraw(lockId)`
- `version()`
- `contractVersion()`
- `positionManager()`
- `lockStatus(lockId)`
- `timeRemaining(lockId)`
- `isLocked(lockId)`
- `isUnlocked(lockId)`
- `isWithdrawn(lockId)`
- `getLock(lockId)`

## Contract Behavior

When a user calls `lock`, the contract transfers the specified LP token amount from the caller into custody and creates an immutable lock record.

When the unlock time is reached, only the designated beneficiary can call `withdraw` to receive the locked LP tokens.

If the lock has already been withdrawn, further withdrawal attempts will fail.

## Lock Status

The contract exposes a status model for off-chain monitoring and analytics.

- `Empty`: the lock ID has never been created.
- `Locked`: the LP tokens are still time-locked.
- `Unlocked`: the unlock time has passed and withdrawal is available.
- `Withdrawn`: the LP tokens have already been released.

## Assumptions

- The LP token is a standard ERC-20 token.
- The LP token supports standard `transferFrom` and `transfer` behavior.
- The beneficiary is able to receive ERC-20 tokens.
- Unlock timing is based on `block.timestamp`.
- The deployment parameters are correct.

## Limitations

- The contract locks only one LP token address.
- It does not support arbitrary ERC-20 assets.
- It does not support Uniswap V3 LP NFTs.
- It does not include emergency recovery functions.
- It does not include an administrative override.

## Events

### LiquidityLocked
Emitted when LP tokens are successfully locked.

### LiquidityWithdrawn
Emitted when LP tokens are released after the unlock time.

These events are intended for explorers, indexers, dashboards, and public verification.

## Audit Notes

The contract follows a simple Checks-Effects-Interactions pattern.

The withdrawn flag is set before the external transfer during withdrawal to reduce reentrancy risk.

The contract is intentionally minimal to reduce attack surface and simplify verification.

